---
import { race } from './models.mjs';
const initial = race(false);
const outcome = (conditional: boolean) => conditional
  ? 'One order accepted for one mug. Arun’s application sees no returned row and tells him the mug is sold out.'
  : 'Two orders accepted for one mug. Both transactions committed, and stock shows 0 as if one mug had been sold.';
---
<figure class="race" data-a00-race aria-labelledby="a00-race-title">
  <figcaption><span class="eyebrow">Figure 3 · illustrative schedule</span><strong id="a00-race-title">Two buyers, one mug</strong></figcaption>
  <div class="controls"><label>Each application <select data-variant><option value="read">Reads stock, then writes what it computed</option><option value="conditional">Sends one conditional UPDATE</option></select></label></div>
  <div class="schedule" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Schedule of the two transactions">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Step</th><th scope="col">Mina’s transaction (order 103)</th><th scope="col">Arun’s transaction (order 104)</th><th scope="col">MUG available, committed</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody data-rows aria-live="polite">{initial.rows.map((row, i) => <tr><td>{i + 1}</td><td>{row.mina}</td><td>{row.arun}</td><td class:list={['stock', { changed: i > 0 && row.stock !== initial.rows[i - 1].stock }]}>{row.stock}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="outcome problem" data-outcome>{outcome(false)}</p>
  <p class="caption">Both transactions run at Read Committed, PostgreSQL’s default isolation level, explained below the figure. Each has already inserted its order and MUG item; only the stock decision is shown. Both schedules were also run as competing sessions on PostgreSQL 18.6, with these outcomes.</p>
  <details><summary>Read this figure as text</summary><p>Reading, then writing: Mina and Arun each read 1, each compute 0 in the application, and each writes 0 and commits. Two orders are accepted for one mug. Conditional UPDATE: Mina’s update changes the row to 0, returns it and locks it until her transaction ends. Arun’s identical update waits for that lock, then rechecks the condition against the committed 0, changes nothing and returns no row, so his application rolls back order 104.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
  import { race } from './models.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-a00-race]').forEach(root => {
    const select = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-variant]')!;
    const body = root.querySelector('[data-rows]')!;
    const outcome = root.querySelector('[data-outcome]')!;
    const cell = (text: string, className = '') => { const td = document.createElement('td'); td.textContent = text; if (className) td.className = className; return td; };
    select.addEventListener('change', () => {
      const conditional = select.value === 'conditional';
      const { rows } = race(conditional);
      body.replaceChildren(...rows.map((row, i) => {
        const tr = document.createElement('tr');
        if (conditional && /wait/.test(row.arun)) tr.className = 'waiting';
        tr.append(cell(String(i + 1)), cell(row.mina), cell(row.arun), cell(row.stock, i > 0 && row.stock !== rows[i - 1].stock ? 'stock changed' : 'stock'));
        return tr;
      }));
      outcome.textContent = conditional
        ? 'One order accepted for one mug. Arun’s application sees no returned row and tells him the mug is sold out.'
        : 'Two orders accepted for one mug. Both transactions committed, and stock shows 0 as if one mug had been sold.';
      outcome.classList.toggle('problem', !conditional);
    });
  });
</script>
<style>
  .race { margin: 2rem 0; border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); padding: 1.2rem; background: var(--color-surface-alt); }
  figcaption strong, figcaption span { display: block; } figcaption strong { font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .controls { margin: 1rem 0; } label { min-width: 0; max-width: 100%; display: flex; gap: .6rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: .85rem; }
  select { font: inherit; color: var(--color-text); background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); border-radius: .3rem; padding: .45rem .7rem; max-width: 100%; }
  select:focus-visible, .schedule:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .schedule { overflow-x: auto; background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); }
  .race table { display: table; width: 100%; margin: 0; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .82rem; }
  .race th, .race :global(td) { border: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule); padding: .5rem .6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  .race th { background: none; font-size: .78rem; }
  .race :global(td:first-child), .race th:first-child { width: 3.5rem; } .race :global(td:last-child), .race th:last-child { width: 6.5rem; }
  .race :global(.stock) { font: 700 .9rem var(--font-mono); }
  .race :global(.changed) { color: var(--color-accent-strong); box-shadow: inset 3px 0 var(--color-accent); }
  .race :global(tr.waiting td:nth-child(3)) { font-style: italic; }
  .outcome { margin: 1rem 0 .5rem; padding: .6rem .8rem; border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--color-accent); background: var(--color-surface); font-size: .9rem; }
  .outcome.problem { border-color: var(--coral); }
  .caption, details { font-size: .8rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); } summary { cursor: pointer; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .race { padding: .8rem; } .race table { font-size: .76rem; } .race th, .race :global(td) { padding: .4rem .35rem; } .race :global(td:first-child), .race th:first-child { width: 2.2rem; } .race :global(td:last-child), .race th:last-child { width: 4.2rem; } }
</style>
